<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Democratic Revolutionary Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1979">1979</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Democratic Revolutionary Party is a Panamanian political party founded in 1979 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omar-torrijos">Omar Torrijos</a> as the political arm of his military regime. It supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a> in the 1980s but, after the American invasion, transformed itself into a democratic centre-left party. It has since won the presidency several times, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernesto-perez-balladares">Ernesto Pérez Balladares</a>, Martín Torrijos and Laurentino Cortizo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/democratic-revolutionary-party.jpg" alt="Democratic Revolutionary Party" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Jacf18 at Wikimedia Commons. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PRD_panama_Party.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
